# ConfigMap hot-reload (default for new FastAPI / Python containers)

When adding or changing a **Python** service deployed under **`k8s/`** that reads configuration from the environment:

1. Prefer a **ConfigMap** plus **`envFrom`** for initial env.
2. Mount the **same** ConfigMap read-only at **`/etc/jarvis/config`** (one file per key).
3. Set **`JARVIS_CONFIG_DIR=/etc/jarvis/config`** and **`JARVIS_CONFIG_RELOAD_INTERVAL_S`** (see **`utils/k8s_config_reload.py`**).
4. On app startup, run **`run_mounted_config_poll_loop`** when **`JARVIS_CONFIG_DIR`** is set; use **`app.state.config_reload_lock`** and an **`on_rebind`** that rebuilds handlers/clients.

Document changes in **`docs/operations/kubernetes-config-hot-reload.md`** and **`docs/reference/environment-variables.md`**.

**Copies:** If the Docker build context is **`asr/`**, **`tts/`**, or **`ui/`**, keep **`k8s_config_reload.py`** in sync with **`utils/k8s_config_reload.py`**.

Non-Python containers (Ollama, Redis, nginx) do **not** use this pattern; use rollout restart or an operator instead.
